post_install() {
	cat <<'MSG'
==> Howdy setup:
    1. Set the camera: `sudo howdy config` -> device_path (list cameras with
       `v4l2-ctl --list-devices` from v4l-utils; prefer an IR camera).
    2. Enrol your face: `sudo howdy add`, then check with `sudo howdy test`.
    3. Add `auth sufficient pam_howdy.so` above the other auth lines of the
       PAM file you want (e.g. /etc/pam.d/sudo or /etc/pam.d/system-auth).
       Never make Howdy the only auth method; keep the password fallback.
    Arch Wiki: https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Howdy
MSG
}
